From: kim.kyeung.pyo <kpkim@gluesys.com>
Subject: [PATCH] prov/verbs: close the dma-buf fd after ibv_reg_dmabuf_mr()

vrb_reg_hmem_dmabuf() obtains a dma-buf file descriptor from
ofi_hmem_get_dmabuf_fd() and hands it to ibv_reg_dmabuf_mr(), but never
closes it. The MR keeps its own reference to the dma-buf, so the fd is
only needed for the duration of the call; leaving it open leaks one fd
per registration.

With the MR cache disabled (e.g. Mercury sets FI_MR_CACHE_MAX_COUNT=0)
every RDMA of GPU memory registers anew, and a process reading 8 GiB in
4 MiB chunks accumulates ~2000 dma-buf fds, hits the default nofile
limit (1024) and cuMemGetHandleForAddressRange() starts failing with
CUDA_ERROR_OPERATING_SYSTEM. Observed with DAOS/Mercury over
verbs;ofi_rxm on H100 + ConnectX-7 (dmabuf-only platform, no peermem):
634 open dma-buf fds after 1.5 s of I/O; 1 after this change.

Close the fd right after the registration attempt, preserving errno for
the failover path.

Signed-off-by: kim.kyeung.pyo <kpkim@gluesys.com>
---
 prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c b/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c
--- a/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c
+++ b/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c
@@
 #include <ofi_util.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include "verbs_ofi.h"
@@ static struct ibv_mr *vrb_reg_hmem_dmabuf(enum fi_hmem_iface iface,
 	mr = ibv_reg_dmabuf_mr(pd, offset, len, (uint64_t)(uintptr_t)buf/* iova */,
 			       fd, vrb_access);
+	/*
+	 * The MR holds its own reference to the dma-buf; keeping the fd open
+	 * leaks one descriptor per registration (fatal for long runs when the
+	 * MR cache is disabled). Preserve errno across close().
+	 */
+	saved_errno = errno;
+	close(fd);
+	errno = saved_errno;
+	saved_errno = 0;
 
 	if (!mr && failover_policy[iface] == TRY &&
 	    vrb_gl_data.peer_mem_support) {
